440
00:49:04,654 --> 00:49:13,840
Those that require a media server will persevere and simply because they will switch to using ISTCP or God forbid, mock, media over quick.

441
00:49:18,446 --> 00:49:36,240
The peer-to-peer ones will have no solution other than going through a server that will relay their data that isn't called a turn and would know what goes inside unless something is built on top, but then you need to trust the one that is doing that to do that implementation.

442
00:49:36,942 --> 00:49:43,440
Whereas today, you trust the browser vendors, which there are a lot less of them, and they're usually more trustful.

